    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="1087" n="1071" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1071"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D128: Black Book, Tab 41: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Far East</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ridgway</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Joint
                        Chiefs of Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-28T19:31:00+09:00">28 October
                            1951—7:31 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CX–56073. Acknowledge your msg nr 85254.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d664-f1"/> When
                    Bradley and Bohlen were here, all were in agreement that when map with our <pb
                        facs="1088" n="1072" xml:id="pg1072"/> proposed demilitarized zone was given
                    to Communists, it would be, with only minor changes, our final offer. Understood
                    this had your full approval. Accordingly, I plan little change in our proposed
                    zone except to reflect further 8th Army advances. Request confirmation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
